    "note": "Freshly reviewed official PyPI/npm metadata and upstream release notes on 2026-10-23 for Git release 0.8.0: hatchling 1.32.4, distlib 0.4.4, packaging 26.3, build 1.6.1, mypy 2.4.0, pytest 9.1.1, pytest-xdist 3.8.0, Ruff 0.17.2, and markdownlint-cli2 0.24.0. All latest non-yanked stable releases satisfy the declared lower bounds; none is excluded. Python 3.14 is explicitly classified except by pytest-xdist, whose >=3.9 metadata permits it; distlib has no Requires-Python field but explicitly classifies 3.14. markdownlint-cli2 requires Node >=22, compatible with the reported rebuilt Node 24.22.0. Reviewed launcher/archive containment fixes, packaging requirement/marker behavior, Hatchling plugin metadata fixes, the build Windows symlink fix, mypy native-parser and macOS x86_64 wheel changes, Ruff 0.17 rule/formatter changes, and markdownlint 0.42 rule updates. No new upper bound or exclusion was identified. This research did not run tests, gates, installation, or clean registry resolution; exact-candidate and native Windows validation remain separate evidence.",
